        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "HMAC-SHA256 relies on a symmetric shared secret known to both the sender and the receiver. If the secret leaks from the consumer, attackers can forge arbitrary webhooks. Ed25519 is an asymmetric public-key signature algorithm (RFC 8032); the sender signs payloads using a private key, and consumers verify signatures using a public key, guaranteeing non-repudiation and zero forgery risk upon consumer compromise."
      }
