      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why is constant-time comparison necessary for webhook signature verification?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Standard string equality operators (==) terminate execution immediately upon finding the first non-matching byte. Attackers can measure execution time differences down to sub-nanosecond intervals to iteratively deduce the expected signature byte-by-byte (timing side-channel attack). Constant-time functions like crypto.timingSafeEqual() compare all bytes regardless of mismatches."
      }
